import{_t as e,it as t,n,rt as r}from"./chunks/framework.BmT8T0yb.js";var i=JSON.parse(`{"title":"Troubleshooting QGC Setup","description":"","frontmatter":{"qt_version":"6.12.0"},"headers":[],"relativePath":"en/qgc-user-guide/troubleshooting/qgc_setup.md","filePath":"en/qgc-user-guide/troubleshooting/qgc_setup.md"}`),a={name:`en/qgc-user-guide/troubleshooting/qgc_setup.md`};function o(n,i,a,o,s,c){return e(),r(`div`,null,[...i[0]||=[t(`<h1 id="troubleshooting-qgc-setup" tabindex="-1">Troubleshooting QGC Setup <a class="header-anchor" href="#troubleshooting-qgc-setup" aria-label="Permalink to “Troubleshooting QGC Setup”">​</a></h1><p>This topic lists troubleshooting information related to <em>QGroundControl</em> setup and installation on the host computer.</p><div class="tip custom-block"><p class="custom-block-title custom-block-title-default">TIP</p><p>Problems when <strong>using</strong> <em>QGroundControl</em> to interact with a vehicle are covered in: <a href="./../troubleshooting/qgc_usage.html">QGC Vehicle Interaction Problems</a>.</p></div><h2 id="opengl_troubleshooting" tabindex="-1">Windows: UI Rendering/Video Driver Issues <a class="header-anchor" href="#opengl_troubleshooting" aria-label="Permalink to “Windows: UI Rendering/Video Driver Issues”">​</a></h2><p>If you experience UI rendering issues or video driver crashes on Windows, this may be caused by &quot;flaky&quot; OpenGL drivers. <em>QGroundControl</em> provides 3 shortcuts that you can use to start <em>QGroundControl</em> in &quot;safer&quot; video modes (try these in order):</p><ul><li><strong>QGroundControl:</strong> QGC uses OpenGL graphics drivers directly.</li><li><strong>GPU Compatibility Mode:</strong> QGC uses ANGLE drivers, which implement OpenGL on top of DirectX.</li><li><strong>GPU Safe Mode:</strong> QGC uses a software rasterizer for the UI (this is very slow). Video is decoded in software too, unless a hardware decoder is selected in the video settings.</li></ul><h2 id="waiting_for_connection" tabindex="-1">Windows: Doesn&#39;t connect to Vehicle over WiFi <a class="header-anchor" href="#waiting_for_connection" aria-label="Permalink to “Windows: Doesn&#39;t connect to Vehicle over WiFi”">​</a></h2><p>If <em>QGroundControl</em> sits forever (for example, <em>Waiting For Vehicle Connection</em>) when trying to connect to the vehicle over Wifi, a possible cause is that IP traffic is being blocked by firewall software (e.g. Windows Defender, Norton, etc.).</p><p>The solution is to allow the <em>QGroundControl</em> app through the firewall.</p><div class="info custom-block"><p class="custom-block-title custom-block-title-default">INFO</p><p>It is possible to simply switch the network profile from Public to Private to allow connections, but this exposes your PC to the Network, so be careful</p></div><p>If using <em>Windows Defender</em>:</p><ul><li><p>In the <strong>Start</strong> bar, enter/select: <em>Firewall &amp; Network Protection</em> (System Settings).</p></li><li><p>Scroll to and select the option: <em>Allow an app through firewall</em>.</p></li><li><p>Select <em>QGroundControl</em> and change the <em>Access</em> selector to <strong>Allow</strong>.</p><div class="tip custom-block"><p class="custom-block-title custom-block-title-default">TIP</p><p>Programs are listed in alphabetical order by description (not filename). You&#39;ll find QGC under <strong>O</strong>: <em>Open source ground control app provided by QGroundControl dev team</em></p></div></li></ul><h2 id="video_troubleshooting" tabindex="-1">Video Does Not Show <a class="header-anchor" href="#video_troubleshooting" aria-label="Permalink to “Video Does Not Show”">​</a></h2><p>The <a href="./../fly_view/fly_view_toolbar.html#video">Video indicator</a> in the Fly View toolbar tells whether a stream arrives: its dropdown shows the bitrate, decoder, display path and packet loss of each stream (see <a href="./../fly_view/video.html#video-statistics">Video Statistics</a>).</p><ul><li><strong>Nothing arrives</strong> (the view says <strong>WAITING FOR VIDEO</strong>, and the dropdown shows no frame rate): check the <strong>Source</strong> and its address in <a href="./../settings_view/video.html">Application Settings &gt; Video</a>, that no other program listens on the same UDP port, and that no firewall blocks the stream (on Windows, allow <em>QGroundControl</em> through the firewall as described <a href="#waiting-for-connection">above</a>). To receive an RTSP stream over TCP, enter its address as <code>rtspt://</code>.</li><li><strong>The stream arrives but has no picture</strong>: <em>QGroundControl</em> says in a message why it can&#39;t decode the stream. When the dropdown names a hardware <strong>Decoder</strong>, set <strong>Force video decoder priority</strong> to <strong>Software</strong>.</li><li><strong>The picture is wrong</strong> (wrong colours, or a green or torn picture): turn on <strong>Force CPU video path</strong>. If that doesn&#39;t help, set <strong>Force video decoder priority</strong> to <strong>Software</strong>.</li><li><strong><em>QGroundControl</em> says at startup that GStreamer failed to initialize</strong>: it plays the streams with Qt Multimedia instead, which the <strong>Video backend</strong> setting can also choose. The application log has the cause.</li></ul><p>These settings are described in <a href="./../settings_view/video.html#settings">Application Settings &gt; Video</a>. When you report a video problem, attach the <a href="./console_logging.html">application log</a>, with the logging categories <code>Video.GStreamer.GstVideoReceiver</code> and <code>Video.VideoManager</code> turned on.</p><p>When a stream played with GStreamer fails or stalls, <em>QGroundControl</em> also saves a graph of its video pipeline as a <code>.dot</code> file in the <code>qgc-pipeline-dot</code> folder of its cache directory (on Linux, under <code>~/.cache/QGroundControl/</code>). It keeps the 10 newest files, and the log names each file it saves. Attach the newest one as well: it shows the pipeline&#39;s elements and formats but not their settings, so it holds no stream address or password.</p>`,17)]])}var s=n(a,[[`render`,o]]);export{i as __pageData,s as default};